    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0234" n="178" xml:id="pg178"/>

                <head>No. 95.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pierrepont to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 18,
                        1876</date>. (Received October 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 18 of August
                    8, 1876, I have the honor to inclose a copy of the correspondence which has
                    taken place between myself and Lord Derby in relation to the case of Edward O’M.
                    Condon, imprisoned under the sentence of a British court, for whom the President
                    of the United States was requested by a joint resolution of Congress to take
                    such steps as might tend to obtain a pardon or release.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARDS PIERREPONT.</signed></closer>




